==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈtɒn.səl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈtɑn.səl/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɒnsəl|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|tonsilla|lang=la}}, compare French {{term|tonsille|lang=fr}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|anatomy|immunology|lang=en}} Either of a pair of small [[mass]]es of [[lymphoid]] [[tissue]] that lie on each side of the [[throat]] and that help [[protect]] the body against [[infection]]; [[palatine tonsil]].
# {{context|anatomy|immunology|lang=en}} Any of various small masses of lymphoid tissues, including [[palatine tonsil]]s, [[adenoid]]s and [[lingual tonsil]]s.

